Article 2 (Approval of and Reporting on Major Policy Matters, etc.)
(1) The Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency and the Commissioner of the National Fire Agency (hereinafter referred to as the "commissioners") shall obtain prior approval from the Minister of the Interior and Safety (hereinafter referred to as the "Minister") on the following matters:
1. Formulation of and changes to basic plans in the policing and fire service fields that require the enactment or amendment of statutes or regulations;
2. Formulation of and changes to major plans concerning international cooperation;
3. Membership in international organizations and conclusion of international agreements.
(2) The commissioners shall report the following matters to the Minister in advance:
1. Matters to be submitted to the State Council;
2. Attendance by a commissioner at an international conference and official overseas trips.
(3) The commissioners shall report the following matters to the Minister:
1. Implementation plans for directions issued by the President, Prime Minister, or Minister, and their implementation results;
2. Results of implementing major policies and plans;
3. Important matters among materials reported or submitted to the President, Prime Minister, and institutions directly under them, the National Assembly, and the Board of Audit and Inspection;
4. Matters relating to major policies among audit results and demands for measures issued by the Board of Audit and Inspection;
5. Other matters requested by the Minister as deemed necessary for the exercise of statutory authority and performance of duties.
